# EXAMPLE crew script: bring up four GPCs and two CRTs through the NBAT to
# OPS 2, waiting on the O6 MODE talkbacks rather than fixed times.  One file
# holds the switches and the keystrokes; panelO6.py plays it (crewscript.py).
# Run from discretePanel/:
#
#   python3 simulatePASS.py --gpcs 1-4 --crts 2 --tape OI340700-v44boot.mmv \
#       --script examples/4gpc-startup.script --duration 900
#
# Every time is written +N: N seconds after the line before (or after the wait
# above it, or after a called script came back), so a line can be inserted
# without renumbering the rest.  Nothing here is a guessed delay: each IPL
# waits for the GPCIPL menu's title to appear on the CRT, and each load for
# that GPC's MODE talkback to read RUN.
#
# IPLing a computer is ONE PROCEDURE DONE FOUR TIMES, so it is written once,
# in ipl-one-gpc.script, and played once per computer with the values that
# differ.  GPC1 is the exception and is still spelled out below: it is the
# first, so the panel's opening setup belongs with it, it uses CRT 1 and the
# left-hand keyboard rather than CRT 2 and KB2, and it is loaded without the
# IDP LOAD toggle the others need.
#
# Verified 2026-09-15: four GPCs to OPS 2, no CAM lamp, MM1 239 commands /
# 2045 blocks read (the same as every earlier verified run).  Each GPCIPL menu
# appeared 13.5 s after its STANDBY and each load took 25-28.5 s, so OPS 2 was
# typed about 363 s after the panel started -- against 570 s when only the
# talkbacks were waited on, and 840 s with fixed times throughout.  Splitting
# the per-GPC procedure out on 2026-09-16 did not change a single action or
# time: it resolves to exactly the sequence that run verified.

# --- all four GPCs to HALT, the IDPs on, GPC1 IPL from MM1 on CRT 1 ---------
+0     gpc 1
+0     mode HALT
+0.01  gpc 2
+0.01  mode HALT
+0.01  gpc 3
+0.01  mode HALT
+0.01  gpc 4
+0.01  mode HALT
+0.02  idppower 1 on
+0.01  idppower 2 on
+0.01  crt 1
+0.1   source MM1
+0.2   gpc 1
+0.1   ipl
+2.5   mode STANDBY
wait crt 1 title GPCIPL timeout 150
+2     keys ITEM 1 EXEC

# --- GPC1 loaded: to RUN -----------------------------------------------------
wait gpc 1 mode-tb RUN timeout 300
+1     crt 0
+2     mode RUN
+2     source OFF

# --- GPC2, 3 and 4: the same procedure, once each, on CRT 2 and KB2 ----------
+5     script ipl-one-gpc.script gpc=2 crt=2 idp=2 kb=KB2
+5     script ipl-one-gpc.script gpc=3 crt=2 idp=2 kb=KB2
+5     script ipl-one-gpc.script gpc=4 crt=2 idp=2 kb=KB2

# --- all four loaded: the NBAT, then OPS 2 -----------------------------------
+11    keys ITEM 1 + 2 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 2 + 1 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 3 + 2 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 4 + 3 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 5 + 4 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 7 + 1 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 8 + 2 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 9 + 3 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 1 0 + 4 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 1 1 + 1 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 1 2 + 1 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 1 3 + 2 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 1 8 + 1 EXEC
+8     keys ITEM 1 9 + 2 EXEC
+21    keys OPS 2 0 1 PRO
